  "term": "military environment",
  "definition": "In this source, a military environment means the operational setting in which soldiers and cadets work and prepare to lead. It is described as changeable, complex, unpredictable, and ambiguous, requiring training for how to act, make decisions, and perform effectively under demanding physical and psychological conditions.",
